buildanagent is open source under four licence terms, one for each kind of
content in the repository.

Code: Apache-2.0 OR MIT, at your option
  Scripts (scripts/), our packages (packages/), the verification harnesses and
  their examples (verify/), the book's code and figure generators (apps/manual/),
  the CI workflows (.github/), the configuration files, and the code blocks in
  the agent skills (.agents/skills/) are licensed under either of

    * the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE), or
    * the MIT License (LICENSE-MIT).

  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 OR MIT

Documentation: CC BY 4.0
  The documents under docs/, the book's prose and figures (apps/manual/), the
  READMEs, the prose of the agent skills (.agents/skills/) and AGENTS.md are
  licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
  (LICENSE-DOCS).

  SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0

Code from the garment engineering textbook: Apache-2.0 only
  Some files in apps/manual/ are copied or adapted from the owner's garment
  engineering textbook (tajistudios/garment-engineering-textbook), with the
  owner's permission. Those files are licensed under the Apache License,
  Version 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE) only, not under the MIT option above. Each one
  opens with a header comment that names its source and this licence, and
  THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md lists each file with its source path and commit.

  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

Mirrored third-party docs: their own licences
  The upstream documentation mirrored under docs/reference/*/source/ is not ours.
  Each mirror keeps its upstream licence file, and its _manifest.json records
  the source repository and the tag or commit it was copied from.
  THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md lists every mirror and its licence.

